{
  "_readme": [
    "Per-locale strings for the shared library browse UI (js/library/library-hub.js).",
    "",
    "Two kinds of string live here, and the distinction matters:",
    "",
    "  labels.types / labels.useCases — the locale's own word for a facet whose",
    "    classification is inherited from the page's English parent. The facet is",
    "    the same fact in every language (a kaomoji page is a kaomoji page); only",
    "    the word shown on the pill is per-locale.",
    "",
    "  labels.platforms — only entries that are ordinary words. Discord, Facebook,",
    "    Instagram, LinkedIn, Snapchat, TikTok, WhatsApp and X are brand names and",
    "    pass through untouched; 'Email' is not a brand and is translated.",
    "  ui — page copy: search box, result count, empty state, back-to-top.",
    "    {shown} and {total} are substituted at render time.",
    "",
    "Nothing else about a hub is translated at build time. Titles, descriptions",
    "and previews are read from each locale page's own markup by",
    "scripts/lib/library-hub-data.js, so a hub cannot carry English its own pages",
    "did not already have.",
    "",
    "",
    "The seven hubs that already had a browse UI (es, fr, id, it, ko, pt, tr)",
    "carry their own inline vocabularies from the 2026-07-14 rollout and are not",
    "listed here; migrating them onto this file is the follow-up that finishes",
    "de-duplicating the template."
  ],
